1353
01:35:13,998 --> 01:35:25,572
我们的第一个方法叫做网状网络，在网状网络中，我们正在创建一个对等节点网络，
它们都将与群组视频通话中的每一个其他对等节点保持点对点连接。
The first approach we have is called a mesh network, and with the mesh network, we are creating a network of peers that will all
maintain a peer-to-peer connection with every other peer inside of a group video call.

1354
01:35:25,760 --> 01:35:28,388
假设我们有一个包含五个对等节点的通话。
So let's say we have a call with five peers.

1355
01:35:28,686 --> 01:35:41,680
那么，对等节点 1 必须与对等节点 2 创建点对点连接，然后是 3、4 和 5，
网络中的所有其他对等节点也必须与该网络中的每一个其他对等节点建立同样的连接。
Well, peer one will have to create a peer-to-peer connection to peer two, then to peer three, four, and five,
and all the other peers in the network will have to create that same connection with every other peer inside of that network.

1356
01:35:42,030 --> 01:35:46,756
所以它就像把它们网状连接在一起，而且这会发生在之后加入的每一个其他对等节点上。
So it kind of meshes them together, and this will happen for every other peer that has to join after this.

1357
01:35:47,150 --> 01:35:53,156
所以每一个新加入的对等节点都必须创建这个连接，
而所有其他对等节点都必须与这个对等节点连接。
So every new peer that joins will have to create this connection, and all the other peers will have to connect back to this peer.

1358
01:35:53,390 --> 01:35:57,892
所以每当一个新的对等节点加入时，我们现在就必须维护一个新的连接。
So every single time a new peer joins, we now have to maintain a new connection.

1359
01:35:58,160 --> 01:36:04,480
从技术上讲，这确实实现了我们在这里需要的功能，
但这种方法有一个巨大的缺点，而且完全无法扩展。
And this technically does accomplish what we need here, but this approach has a massive downside and does not scale at all.

1360
01:36:04,686 --> 01:36:10,820
这里的问题是，每当一个新的对等节点加入时，我们现在就必须上传我们的流并维护那个连接。
The problem here is that every single time a new peer joins, we now have to upload our stream and maintain that connection.

1361
01:36:11,182 --> 01:36:13,572
所以这需要大量的上行带宽。
So this requires a lot of upload bandwidth.

1362
01:36:13,680 --> 01:36:18,240
所以一旦你超过 4 到 5 个对等节点，你就会开始看到很多问题。
So once you go beyond four to five peers, you're gonna start seeing a lot of issues here.

1363
01:36:18,350 --> 01:36:21,476
所以如果你想进行扩展，就不推荐这种方法。
So this approach is not recommended if you're looking to scale.

1364
01:36:21,966 --> 01:36:32,480
现在我们要讨论的第二种方法，不是点对点架构，而是更偏向点对服务器架构，
也就是 多会议单元 方法，代表多会议单元。
Now the second approach we're going to talk about is less of a peer-to-peer architecture and more of a peer-to-server architecture,
and that is the MCU approach, which stands for multi-conferencing unit.

1365
01:36:32,640 --> 01:36:42,560
它的工作原理是，现在每个对等节点都会连接到服务器，而且与网状网络不同，
我们会把流上传到那个服务器上，服务器会接收所有进入的
So how this works is now each peer will be connected to the server, and unlike the mesh network,
we're going to upload our stream to that server, and that server will take in all the incoming streams, process them,

1366
01:36:42,560 --> 01:36:43,840
流，对它们进行处理、混合，然后再发回给各个对等节点。
So how this works is now each peer will be connected to the server, and unlike the mesh network,
we're going to upload our stream to that server, and that server will take in all the incoming streams, process them,

1367
01:36:43,840 --> 01:36:46,788
流，对它们进行处理、混合，然后再发回给各个对等节点。
mix them together, and then send them back to the peers.

1368
01:36:47,150 --> 01:36:52,068
这种方法的优点是扩展性更好，而且你只需要上传一次流。
Now, the upside to this is that it does scale better, and you only have to upload your stream once.

1369
01:36:52,462 --> 01:37:05,636
缺点是，你发送数据的那个服务器必须非常强悍，因为它得处理所有这些内容，
所以实际处理起来可能会非常昂贵。也就是说，它扩展性更好，但缺点是成本更高。
The downside is that that server that you're gonna send this to has to be very beefy, it has to process all of this,
so it could get very expensive to actually handle this, so it scales better, but the downside is that it's gonna be more expensive.

1370
01:37:06,094 --> 01:37:16,350
对于第三种也是最后一种方法，我们有 选择性转发单元 方法，代表选择性转发单元。
